      "title": "Part-Time Faculty Pool- Chemistry (2026-2027)",
      "description": "Part-Time Faculty Pool- Chemistry (2026-2027) - Glenside, PA - Arcadia University Jobs Jobs Login Back to all jobs Part-Time Faculty Pool- Chemistry (2026-2027) Posted 29-Sep-2022 (EST) 450 South Easton Road, Glenside, PA, USA Email Me Similar Jobs Email Me This Job 2026-2027 Arcadia University invites applications for Adjunct Professors (part time) in the Department of Chemistry and Physics. The number of part-time instructors hired by the department varies from semester to semester, depending upon the needs of the program. When a position is available, qualified applicants may be contacted for an interview and asked to submit further documentation. While there may not be immediate openings, the hiring manager will review applications when openings do occur. Responsibilities : Candidates are expected to teach one or more of the following: introductory general chemistry lectures and/or laboratories, organic chemistry laboratories, biochemistry, advanced inorganic, polymers, instrumental analysis, depending on qualifications. Qualifications: Candidates should possess a Master's Degree in chemistry or a closely related field (minimum). Course credits vary but normally between 3-4 credits a class. Lab courses are 2 credits each. A link to our most recent Collective Bargaining Agreement: https://www.arcadia.edu/about-arcadia/leadership/office-provost/collective-bargaining-agreement/ Application Instructions : Applications must be submitted online through Arcadia's Human Resources portal to receive full consideration. Please do not email application materials to the hiring manager. Due to the volume of applications received, communication will generally be limited to candidates selected for additional consideration. Application review will begin immediately. Posting will be removed from the website once we've established a sufficient talent pool for consideration. Arcadia University is a top-ranked private University in Greater Philadelphia that pro